## Re-fetching

To re-fetch and verify the SHA-256 values match this record:

    SHA=f9fc9a936e3f3bb50fc001de638b36b94a87b5ca
    BASE=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Forceflow/cuda_voxelizer/$SHA
    for f in src/voxelize.cu src/voxelize.cuh src/morton_LUTs.h src/util.h LICENSE; do
        curl -fsSL --max-time 30 "$BASE/$f" | sha256sum
    done

Expected output (order matches the loop; compare against the table above):

    9acf0463d6d4ee0eb89a3bd70fd9d5c48c68b0930537315e5fa809a6cfe86bd7  -   (voxelize.cu)
    8cf320665a3e4d018c2b7dc1ed2df3bc55bd3adb5d12da49b32746ee20163172  -   (voxelize.cuh)
    87088dbcf176508b4816affca3b0bd7d2e5f9c1a611dbfc167b8938b1de62154  -   (morton_LUTs.h)
    4b2525a882e12f0595e7d6d561af22d3c8009cfb523d6694de301dbd77b50980  -   (util.h)
    a5a9e693ff99c8ad0cae7ca222e93f4255268d4895996ca6d62ced8e8946dde2  -   (LICENSE)

If any SHA differs, upstream has been updated since 2026-07-04 and the
project must re-validate the SHA-pin per `research/gpu_port_proposal.md`
